⟦ task_spec | VSL-LANG-REV-TASK-SPEC-v0.1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-12T10:07:22Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status ratified
// sandbox/vsl-language-rev/TASK_SPEC.vsm — TASK ROOT of the vsl_language
// revision proposal. Read THIS FIRST, then descend into the subdirs.
// Audience: the parent (vsf-s3-validator) reviewing for promotion. Also rmw3.
// STATUS: sandbox proposal — NOT canon. Promotion is the parent's decision.

task_spec("VSL-LANG-REV-TASK-SPEC") {

  // ════ WHAT THIS TASK IS ════
  // TOKEN-COUNT METHOD (R1, reconciled 2026-08-12): tiktoken cl100k_base
  //   (python3 -c 'import tiktoken; enc=tiktoken.get_encoding("cl100k_base")').
  //   canon=24,374 tok ▪ primer=4,899 tok ▪ reference_set=13,809 tok ▪
  //   reduction(primer/canon)=-79.9% ▪ reduction(primer+set/canon)=-23.2%.
  what: "
    Split the canonical boot/vsl_language.vsm (24,374 tok tiktoken cl100k_base,
    1517 lines) into a WRITING CORE (compact primer, 4,899 tok, -79.9%) + a
    REFERENCE SET of 14 small per-item .vsm files (13,809 tok total, ~986 tok avg (13,809/14)
    each on average, readable on demand). The agent that needs only to WRITE
    VSL reads the primer (+ core_boot_primer passed by reference); the agent
    needing a NON-writing item (a definition, a gate, the PSI protocol) opens
    the one relevant file, not the whole 24K-tok doc.",

  // ════ WHY ════
  why: "
    The 24,374-tok vsl_language.vsm conflates two audiences: writers (need 4 axioms,
    grammar, types, C1/C5/C6 closure) and reference operators (need D7 opsroom,
    PSI/VSI ladders, validation gates, glossary of theory defs). Loading the
    full doc for every read is the boot-budget problem. The split lets the boot
    package stay light while operator-grade material remains accessible — one
    item per file, cited not duplicated from the already-canonical core.",

  // ════ THE TWO DELIVERABLES ════
  deliverables: "
    1. boot/vsl_language_primer.vsm — the WRITING CORE (compressed). Owns:
       substrate summary ▪ A1-A11 (one-line) ▪ grammar ▪ types ▪ labels for
       validator use ▪ C1/C5/C6 CLOSEURE gates ▪ status_enum ▪ minimal envelope
       ACT form ▪ tick(L). 4,899 tok (tiktoken cl100k_base). Status: proposed.
    2. s5-policy/vsl-language/index.vsm + 14 items — the REFERENCE SET. Owns the
       NON-writing items: axioms A12-A15 ▪ definitions D5-D21 split core/theory
       ▪ validation_gates ▪ memory+machine ▪ m2m+P2 crypto ▪ norm+response_class
       ▪ PSI ▪ VSI ▪ standardization tooling ▪ encyclopedia ▪ reframe() ▪
       scope/changelog. Each item: ONE file, cited not re-stated, source § pointed
       to boot/vsl_language.vsm. 13,809 tok total (tiktoken cl100k_base);
       primer+set = 18,708 tok = -23.2% vs canon." ,

  // ════ RELATION TO CANON (what the parent reviews) ════
  relation_to_canon: "
    Source-of-truth: docs/spec_revision/system/boot/vsl_language.vsm (UNCHANGED,
      canonical, 1517 lines). The primer + reference set are DERIVATIONS:
      every statement is CITED to a § of the source, not re-stated.
    not canon: these sandbox files carry @status ratified. They are NOT applied
      as spec until promoted; the canonical source remains the active spec.
    Promotion target: docs/spec_revision/system/ — primer → boot/, set →
      s5-policy/vsl-language/. Promotion REPLACES nothing the primer already
      shares with core_boot_primer (those are cross-referenced, not duplicated).",

  // ════ HOW TO REVIEW (gate sequence for the parent) ════
  review_protocol: "
    1. Read THIS file (task scope + deliverables).
    2. Read s5-policy/vsl-language/index.vsm (the manifest — file tree, item
       map, dependency order, validation gate).
    3. Spot-check 3-4 items against their cited source § (each file's header
       names its source §). The claim: verbatim or faithful précis, not paraphrase
       drift. Flag any item where the précis diverges from source §.
    4. Run the per-file gate (scripts/vsl/):
         tokenizer --check <file>      — structure (balanced blocks)
         verify_encoding <file>        — UTF-8/NFC/no-BOM/4-field header
         vslline --selftest            — line discipline (9/9)
       All 14 files + the primer pass (see session block in child TASKS.vsm).
    5. Decide: promote / hold / rework. Promotion mandate:
         (a) @status ratified → ratified on the promoted copy
         (b) D7 English-pass on s5-policy/ items (prose-language hygiene)
         (c) corpus symbol_table clean once the items land in docs/spec_revision/
    ",
  // ════ DIRECTORY LAYOUT (the 'one task one dir' convention) ════
  layout: "
    vsl-language-rev/
      TASK_SPEC.vsm           ← THIS file (task root: specs, considerations,
                                 instructions for the parent)
      boot/                   ← writing-core slice
        vsl_language_primer.vsm
      s5-policy/
        vsl-language/        ← reference-set slice (mirrors the home it targets)
          index.vsm          ← manifest
          (14 item files)
      scripts/               ← [-- empty placeholder; if task-internal scripts
                                 are added later, they live here --]
      logs/                  ← [-- empty placeholder; if logs are needed,
                                 they live here --]",

  // ════ CONSIDERATIONS (the judgements that made the parent's job easier/harder) ════
  considerations: "
    • Merges (not the original 15-file tree): three pairs merged into single files
      — memory+machine → memory_machine.vsm; m2m+P2crypto → comms_extension.vsm;
      norm+response_class → norm_response_class.vsm. Reason: both halves of each
      pair are <0.6K tok and share a conceptual frame; separate files added a
      hop with no readability gain. Flag if the parent prefers the original split.
    • Definitions split (not one 3.5K-tok dictionary): core (D5-D13+D11b, ~1.8K) +
      theory (D14-D21 addendum, ~1.4K). Reason: D14-D21 are theory-proof
      consumers (composition_proof, dynamics_choice, vos_proofs) — a separate
      audience from the operational D5-D13. The single-file version exceeded
      'readable in one shot' heavily; both halves now still exceed 1.2K but
      are REFERENCE dictionaries (the index gate exempts those, matching the
      source doc's own note on the original D5-D21).
    • @ref pointers in memory_machine.vsm are verbatim from source §10 (they
      ILLUSTRATE the @ref convention, not a dangling reference in this set).
    • The primer's SOURCE is the unchanged canonical doc. If the canonical
      doc is revised, the primer + set need a re-read pass (the staleness gate
      catches this once promoted, not in the sandbox).",
}
⟦ /task_spec ⟧